Round interview

**1. What happened**

On level 4 the socket is behind a gate. The gate opens only when a shrunk piece, standing directly under a narrow channel and facing up, fires a beam that destroys a box at the top. The timer, even with its one refill item, allows about 26 actions. My best route needs about 29, so it has died 3 moves from the socket twice.

This attempt I spent the whole timer checking whether some hidden 3×3 panel pattern exists that could save actions. I changed one panel cell per click so every click tested a new combination. I tried level 2's teleport pattern, diagonals, an X, the corners, the outer ring, the full grid, a plus sign and others. Nothing triggered, and the timer ran out. It failed because the attempt was spent on exploration, and the exploration found nothing.

**2. Can it be beaten?**

I can't tell. I claim no route built from the mechanics I've found fits the timer.

These parts are established, each observed at least twice:
- **Timer:** 64 rows; about 3.5 rows per move or click, about 6 for a pattern-completing click. The refill gives back about 36 rows, once, collected only by the shrunk piece. Two identical full runs died on action 26.
- **Gate:** it opens only via the shrunk beam from x31 facing up, and facing is set by the last move. It blocks both piece sizes. The full-size beam at x29 fails. A beam aimed at the gate does nothing.
- **Positions:** the full-size piece can only stand at x and y values 1 more than a multiple of 4, which never puts it on the refill or under the channel. Shrinking keeps the top-left quarter; growing puts the shrunk piece in the bottom-right quarter.
- **Patterns:** they must match exactly; only shrink/grow and fire exist among the roughly 15 sets I tested; the panel resets after each trigger. Clicks outside the panel only flash it and cost nothing.

The fewest actions I can build:
- 6 moves to put the shrunk piece on the refill;
- 5 moves to stand under the channel, facing up, at the height that regrows into the gate row;
- 7 moves from there to the socket;
- 11 clicks (shrink, fire, grow).

That is about 29 actions. Every alternative I worked out costs as much or more:
- firing before taking the refill (the timer empties before reaching it);
- staying shrunk after firing;
- regrowing to line up a full-size shot;
- shrinking at the start;
- hitting the refill with the beam instead of walking to it.

What I haven't checked:
- whether a full-size beam from x31 works (my routes using it are still longer);
- whether partially entering the socket wins (saves at most 1);
- the remaining untested panel combinations;
- whether hitting the refill with the beam collects it.

Because the level was presumably designed to be solvable, I still expect some mechanic is missing. I just have no concrete candidate left.

**3. Next attempt**

I'll run the best route as tightly as possible, then check the last cheap unknowns:
- fire the beam at the refill item, to see whether it collects it from a distance;
- test whether partially entering the socket counts as a win.

I'll log the exact timer cost of every action.

VERDICT: undecided
CONFIDENCE: 15
